Taskora — Productivity Landing Page

Plan better. Focus deeper. Make progress every day.

Taskora is a clean, modern, and responsive productivity landing page designed around the idea that meaningful progress starts with clear priorities and consistent action.

The project showcases a productivity platform concept that encourages users to organize their tasks, manage their time, and focus on what matters most. It was built as a frontend practice project to strengthen my HTML and CSS skills while learning to create visually appealing and user-friendly web experiences.

✨ Features
Modern UI Design: A clean layout with a consistent color palette and clear visual hierarchy.
Hero Section: A welcoming introduction to Taskora and its purpose.
Features Section: Highlights the benefits of staying organized and focused.
How It Works: Presents a simple approach to planning and completing tasks.
About Section: Explains the philosophy behind Taskora.
Call-to-Action Sections: Encourages visitors to take the next step.
Responsive Layout: Designed to adapt to desktop, tablet, and mobile screens.
🛠️ Technologies Used
HTML5
CSS3
CSS Grid and Flexbox
CSS Media Queries
Responsive Web Design
🎯 Project Goals

The goal of this project is to improve my frontend development skills through practical implementation, focusing on semantic HTML, reusable CSS styling, responsive layouts, and clean user interface design.

📚 What I Learned

While building Taskora, I practised:

Structuring web pages with semantic HTML.
Creating layouts with CSS Grid and Flexbox.
Styling sections with consistent spacing, typography, and colors.
Making layouts responsive across different screen sizes.
Organizing project files for easier maintenance.
